# Command defuddle

## What does this command do:

Defuddle is an open-source tool that extracts core content from web pages by stripping away clutter like sidebars and ads into clean HTML or Markdown. It has consistent output and extensive metadata extraction across browsers, Node.js, and CLI environments.

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: `npm install -g defuddle`
For Raspberry Pi install using: `npm install -g defuddle`
For Mac install using: `npm install -g defuddle`

## Command path

For Fedora run: `defuddle`
For Raspberry Pi run: `defuddle`
For Mac run: `/opt/homebrew/bin/defuddle`

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://github.com/kepano/defuddle

## YouTube video text (transcripts)

Defuddle cannot extract transcript text from YouTube pages. Use `yt-dlp` instead.

### Step 1 — check what captions are available

    yt-dlp --list-subs <URL>

### Step 2a — download captions only (fast, no video)

    # Auto-generated captions (English), output as SRT
    yt-dlp --skip-download --write-auto-subs --sub-langs "en" --sub-format "srt" \
        -o "%(title)s.%(ext)s" <URL>

    # Prefer manual captions, fall back to auto-generated
    yt-dlp --skip-download --write-subs --write-auto-subs --sub-langs "en" --sub-format "srt" \
        -o "%(title)s.%(ext)s" <URL>

Output file will be named `<video-title>.en.srt`.

### Step 2b — strip SRT timestamps → plain text

    sed '/^[0-9][0-9]*$/d; /^[0-9:,]* --> /d; /^$/d; s/<[^>]*>//g' video.en.srt > video.txt

### Step 3 — convert plain text to Markdown (optional)

Pipe through defuddle is not applicable here. Just use the `.txt` or wrap in a `.md` header manually.

### Fallback — no captions available: download audio + Whisper

    # Download audio only
    yt-dlp --skip-download --extract-audio --audio-format wav -o "%(title)s.%(ext)s" <URL>
    # Or download video then extract audio with ffmpeg
    yt-dlp -o "%(title)s.%(ext)s" <URL>
    ffmpeg -i "video.mp4" -vn -ac 1 -ar 16000 -c:a pcm_s16le audio.wav

    # Transcribe with faster-whisper (install: pip install --user faster-whisper)
    python3 -c "
    from faster_whisper import WhisperModel
    model = WhisperModel('small', device='cpu', compute_type='int8')
    segs, _ = model.transcribe('audio.wav', vad_filter=True)
    print('\n'.join(s.text.strip() for s in segs))
    " > transcript.txt

## Command options

# Parse a local HTML file:
defuddle parse <file.html>

# Parse a URL:
defuddle parse <https://example.com/article>

# Output as Markdown:
defuddle parse <input> --markdown

# Output as JSON with metadata:
defuddle parse <input> --json

# Extract a specific property (e.g. title, description, domain):
defuddle parse <input> --property <name>

# Write output to a file instead of stdout:
defuddle parse <input> --output <file>

# Set preferred language (BCP 47, e.g. en, fr, ja):
defuddle parse <input> --lang <code>

# Enable debug mode:
defuddle parse <input> --debug
